# Schedules are UTC.
#
# vercel.json's `crons` block (same three routes, same cadence) only takes effect when this app is
# actually hosted on Vercel — this deployment runs as a plain Docker container behind Traefik
# (see docker-compose.yaml), where that file is inert. Without this cron container none of these
# routes were ever called on a schedule; each only ran when an admin triggered it by hand (e.g.
# the admin settings page's "Refresh rate now" button for usd-pkr-rate). Mirrors ilmai.study's own
# services/cron container, which hit this exact bug first.
0 */6 * * * curl -fsS --retry 3 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_INTERNAL_URL/api/cron/usd-pkr-rate"
0 * * * * curl -fsS --retry 2 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_INTERNAL_URL/api/cron/abandoned-cart"
*/15 * * * * curl -fsS --retry 2 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$APP_INTERNAL_URL/api/cron/release-inventory"
